[ASSUMED-5]: Enterprise shippers (multinational FMCG and manufacturing companies) operating in Indonesia, Thailand, and Vietnam would pay $500–$2,000/month for a SEA-specific carrier compliance monitoring tool if one existed with API connectivity to national registries — to validate: ask five SEA-market procurement and supply chain directors at multinational manufacturers what they currently spend on carrier risk management in SEA and whether they would fund a new solution.

